# The auto-configurations @LudwigGrpcServerTest boots: this starter, whole, and the two web-core
# auto-configurations it cannot run without (the problem registry and the preference resolver).
# Whole on purpose - a slice that left out the security auto-configuration would pass tests that
# production fails, which is worse than having no slice.
#
# The optional integrations are listed too. Each is behind @ConditionalOnClass and a bean
# condition, so a slice test gets exactly the stages its classpath and its own beans call for:
# a JwtDecoder bean turns authentication on, and without one the test says
# ludwig.grpc.server.security.enabled=false, as a service would have to.
ru.ludwigandreas.webcore.config.WebCoreProblemAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.webcore.config.WebCorePreferenceAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.grpc.server.config.GrpcServerAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.grpc.server.config.GrpcServerSecurityAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.grpc.server.config.GrpcServerObservabilityAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.grpc.server.config.GrpcServerIdempotencyAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.grpc.server.config.GrpcServerAdminAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.grpc.server.config.GrpcServerTestAutoConfiguration
